    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i've already checked the agent resources and they look pretty stable. i'm also pretty sure it's not a database timeout because the logs don't show any connectivity drops. it just seems like there's something weird going on under the hood that i can't track down. do you think it could be something related to how the containers are spinning up or maybe some weird race condition in the environment setup?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If resources and external services are fine, containerization issues or race conditions are strong next suspects. Examine the Docker build logs and startup scripts very closely for timing dependencies that might not be obvious in the application logs. You might need to introduce explicit, short `sleep()` commands around critical setup steps to see if that stabilizes the intermittent failures. Pinpointing where the timing difference occurs between local and CI execution is key to solving this.",
      "source": "target",
