    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, i tried adding some sleeps in a few spots and it helped for a bit but then the flakiness came right back. it's like there are these tiny little glitches that just pop up out of nowhere and mess everything up. it feels so random, like something is actively sabotaging the build every once in a while. any other way to catch these tiny inconsistencies?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since simple sleeps only offer temporary fixes, you need more aggressive logging during the setup phase. Increase the verbosity of your container tooling and test runner to capture extremely low-level execution details. Consider introducing distributed tracing or more detailed logging across the components to watch for brief moments of high load or resource contention that aren't visible in standard metrics. This deeper visibility might expose the pattern behind the perceived randomness.",
      "source": "target",
